title: 'hrmp: give back the open request deposits of an offboarding para'
doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    When a para offboards, the deposits of its channels are given back to its account, but the
    deposits of its pending open channel requests were kept reserved, with nothing left to release
    them. The request cleanup now gives back both deposits of a removed request, including those of
    the outgoing para itself.

    This changes behaviour specified in the implementers' guide, which said deposits of the
    outgoing para are not returned; the guide is updated accordingly.

    No storage, API or configuration change. Deposits already left reserved by earlier versions
    are not touched.
crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: patch
